# webOS TV's embedded Chromium lags years behind desktop Chrome (webOS 6 ships
# Chromium ~79, which predates optional chaining / nullish coalescing support
# added in Chromium 80). Without this file Angular's esbuild builder assumes a
# modern target and emits that syntax unlowered, which fails to parse at all on
# the TV — a silent blank screen, since a module script parse error produces no
# visible output. Floor set low enough to cover webOS 4/5/6 TVs, not just this one.
Chrome >= 70
